use std
into local_shadow_check.amni

Imports: os, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes and gfx.scene3d. A standalone GPU program that checks shadows from point lights in the shared local shadow atlas and prints one line per check, then "local: ok" when all pass or "local: FAILED" when any fails. These already exist; never define them here: `gfx::open_headless(w, h) bool`, `gfx::error()`, `gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`, `gfx::flush()`, `gfx::grab(texture)` (a struct with int fields `w` and `h` and the byte list `px`, four bytes per pixel, red first), `gfx::translate(float3) gfx::mat4`, `gfx::mat4_identity`; `shapes::material(rgb float3, metallic f32, roughness f32) gltf::Material`, `shapes::plane(half f32, m) int`, `shapes::cube(half float3, m) int`, `shapes::sphere(radius f32, around int, down int, m) int` (each gives an asset); `s3d::add(asset) int` (an item), `s3d::place(item, gfx::mat4)`, `s3d::init(w, h)`, `s3d::render(target)`, `s3d::local_stats() int, int` (faces drawn into the atlas by the last frame, then faces that were due), the module vars `s3d::lights` (a growable list of `s3d::Light`, a struct with fields `pos` float3, `range` f32, `rgb` float3, `kind` int, `radius` f32, `shadows` bool and `soft` f32; build it with `s3d::Light { pos: p, range: r, rgb: c, kind: 0, radius: 0.02, shadows: true, soft: 0.0, .. }`), `s3d::frame_u.light_shd` (16 float4: x below 0 means that light got no shadow), `s3d::local_ts` (int list, three per face: atlas x, atlas y and size, size 0 when unused), `s3d::local_used` (int, faces in use), `s3d::local_cache` (bool), `s3d::rt_shadows` (bool), `s3d::debug_view` (int), `s3d::view` (an `s3d::Camera { eye: e, target: t, up: u, fov_y: f, near: n, far: d }`), `s3d::sun` (fields `rgb` float3 and `shadows` bool), `s3d::sky` (fields `ambient` f32 and `draw` bool) and `s3d::look` (fields `bloom` f32, `ssao` bool, `curve` int). Time with `clock_ns()` (an int of nanoseconds from the os import, called bare: `os::clock_ns` and `os::clock` do not exist). A module bool `failed` starts false; `check(name, ok, detail)` prints "PASS " or "FAIL " then the name, then " (" the detail ")" when the detail is not empty, and sets `failed` when ok is false. Write reals in details with `format_flt`.

Scene, 512 by 512: a floor `shapes::plane(4.0, ...)` of grey 0.6 with roughness 0.9 at the origin; 16 pillars, pillar i a `shapes::cube` of half size (0.08, 0.3, 0.08) placed by `gfx::translate` at (x, 0.3, z) with x = -2.25 + 1.5 times (i mod 4) and z = -2.25 + 1.5 times (i div 4), grey 0.6 roughness 0.9, each with a sphere of radius 0.14 (48 around, 24 down, the same material) on top at (x, 0.75, z); 16 point lights, light i at (x + 0.3, 1.25, z + 0.2) of its pillar (above its ball, so the ball and pillar throw wide shadows on the floor), range 2.0, rgb (0.5, 0.5, 0.5), soft 0, shadows on. Keep the pillar items in a list. Sun rgb zero and its shadows off, sky ambient 0 and draw false, bloom 0, ssao off, curve 1, `debug_view` 5 (direct light only). The camera looks from (0, 7, 4) at the origin with up (0, 1, 0), fov_y 0.9, near 0.05, far 50. `s3d::init(512, 512)` and one render target. `shot()` renders 3 frames (each `s3d::render` then `gfx::flush`) and returns the grabbed pixels' luminance per pixel as a real list (0.2126 red plus 0.7152 green plus 0.0722 blue).

L1 room: after `shot()` with every light shadowed, count the lights whose `light_shd` x is at least 0; pass when 16 of 16; detail the count and the faces in use.

L2 matches ray tracing: A is `shot()` with the atlas; then every light's shadows off and `s3d::rt_shadows` on gives R; then rt off and shadows off gives C (no shadows). Over pixels where C is above 2: the error is the sum of the absolute differences of A and R over the sum of C, and the agreement is the share of those pixels where (A below 0.5 times C) equals (R below 0.5 times C). Pass when the error is at most 0.05 and the agreement at least 0.97; detail both with four decimals. Control: the same error between C and R must be above 0.01 (shadows are visible in this scene) and at least ten times the error of A (the atlas is ten times closer to ray tracing than no shadows at all), printed as its own check "L2c control sees shadows" with the control error and that ratio, both with four decimals (the ratio with one). Turn every light's shadows back on and rt off after.

L3 cache: render one frame, then 10 more frames with nothing moving, summing the first number of `local_stats` over those 10; pass when the sum is 0. Control "L3c no cache redraws": with `local_cache` false one frame draws `local_used` faces; set it back to true after.

L4 moving caster: move pillar 0 by 0.3 in x (place it again), render one frame and read the faces drawn; pass when it is at least 1 and at most 12 (only lights within range of that pillar redraw). Then A is `shot()`, then with `local_cache` false B is `shot()` and `local_cache` true again; pass "L4b cached equals fresh" when the largest absolute difference between A and B is at most 1.0; detail it.

L5 sizes follow the screen: set `s3d::local_min` to 32 (so far lights may shrink below the default floor of 128), render once, take the mean of the sizes of the used faces now, then with the camera eye at (0, 28, 16) after one render; pass when the far mean is at most half of the near mean; detail both. Put the camera back and `s3d::local_min` back to 128.

L6 cost: render 10 warm frames; time 30 frames (`s3d::render` plus `gfx::flush` each) with the cache on, then 30 with `local_cache` false, then set it true; pass when the cached mean is below 0.7 times the uncached mean; detail both means in milliseconds with two decimals.

`main` opens the device (print "local: no device: " and `gfx::error()` and return when it fails), builds the scene, runs L1 to L6 and prints "local: ok" or "local: FAILED".
